timer.dom - the G1.1 fixture, in nb_serialize() wire format.

NOT HTML, and that is the whole lesson of the last three commits.
nb_dom_load() does not parse markup: it reads the serializer's own
stream and returns NULL unless the first byte of the file is 'N'
(nb_dom.c). So:

  - an HTML fixture  -> empty DOM, STATUS ok, one TITLE row
  - this file with a single "#" comment line at the top -> empty DOM,
    STATUS ok, one TITLE row, identically

Both failures are SILENT, which is why this cost so long: the harness
kept reporting "the worker never rendered the page" in exactly the words
a real G1 failure would use.

The format, from nb_dom.c's serialize_rec():
    N|tag|id|cls|<textlen>|<text>|<attrslen>|<attrs>
    D before children, U after
The page this describes is in timer.html - which is what a fetcher would
have saved. What the WORKER consumes is this file.
